From: System Electronics
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 17:10:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] drm/bridge: cdns-dsi: diagnostic delay before enabling video

Diagnostic only, inert by default. The kernel parameter
cdns_dsi.video_delay_ms=N sleeps N ms in cdns_dsi_bridge_enable(), after
the wait for the clock and data lanes and before VID_EN and the panel
enable: the spot where the build before 0017 spent its 262 ms.

Unlike cdns_dphy.cal_wait_time=0, this adds time only and keeps the short
PHY calibration. The two parameters together separate "the display chain
needs time at boot" from "the PHY needs the long calibration".

No log line on purpose, same reason as 0019. The value in use is in
/sys/module/cdns_dsi/parameters/video_delay_ms.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [diagnostic, to be removed]

---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/cdns-dsi.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/cdns-dsi.c
@@ -14,6 +14,7 @@
 #include <video/mipi_display.h>
 
 #include <linux/clk.h>
+#include <linux/delay.h>
 #include <linux/interrupt.h>
 #include <linux/iopoll.h>
 #include <linux/ktime.h>
@@ -788,6 +789,10 @@
 	dsi->link_initialized = true;
 }
 
+static unsigned int video_delay_ms;
+module_param(video_delay_ms, uint, 0444);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(video_delay_ms, "Diagnostic: delay in ms before enabling video, after the lanes are ready");
+
 static void cdns_dsi_bridge_enable(struct drm_bridge *bridge)
 {
 	struct cdns_dsi_input *input = bridge_to_cdns_dsi_input(bridge);
@@ -834,6 +839,9 @@
 			 "DSI-DPhy Clock and Data Lanes ready after %lld us\n",
 			 phy_wait_us);
 
+	if (video_delay_ms)
+		msleep(video_delay_ms);
+
 	writel(HBP_LEN(dsi_cfg.hbp) | HSA_LEN(dsi_cfg.hsa),
 	       dsi->regs + VID_HSIZE1);
 	writel(HFP_LEN(dsi_cfg.hfp) | HACT_LEN(dsi_cfg.hact),
